                "senderName": "NWS Upton NY",
                "headline": "Heat Advisory issued August 9 at 2:24PM EDT until August 10 at 7:00PM EDT by NWS Upton NY",
                "description": "* WHAT...Heat index values up to 98.\n\n* WHERE...Bronx, Kings (Brooklyn), New York (Manhattan), Northern\nQueens, Richmond (Staten Island), and Southern Queens Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 7 PM EDT Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Hot temperatures and high humidity may cause heat\nillnesses.",
                "instruction": "A Heat Advisory is issued when the combination of heat and humidity\nis expected to make it feel like it is 95 to 99 degrees for two or\nmore consecutive days, or 100 to 104 degrees for any length of time.\n\nSeniors and those with chronic health problems or mental health\nconditions are at an increased risk. Homes without air conditioning\ncan be much hotter than outdoor temperatures.\n\nUse air conditioning to stay cool at home or go to a place that has\nair conditioning. If you don't have home air conditioning, continue\nto seek out cool spaces each day as long as it remains hot, and for a\nfew days after if your home is still hot. Check on vulnerable\nfriends, family members and neighbors.\n\nTo reduce risk during outdoor work, the Occupational Safety and\nHealth Administration recommends scheduling frequent rest breaks in\nshaded or air conditioned environments. Anyone overcome by heat\nshould be moved to a cool and shaded location. Heat stroke is an\nemergency! In cases of heat stroke call 9 1 1.",
